From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: max77705: UNO regulator for reverse wireless charging

The boost can feed the UNO output instead of CHGIN (mode 0x8), which
powers the wireless charger chip as a transmitter. Register it as a
regulator, 5 to 9 V on VBYPSET and 0.2 to 1.5 A on UNOILIM, with stock's
rules: refused while OTG, a cable or a pad has the charger; switched off
when a cable comes in, OTG starts or the bypass current limit trips, and
the consumer is told with REGULATOR_EVENT_FORCE_DISABLE.

The CNFG_00 mode field now has a lock, and charge enable leaves it
alone while UNO runs: OR-ing the charge bit into 0x8 gives 0x9.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/maxim,max77705.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/maxim,max77705.yaml
index 190aa71..8f9173f 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/maxim,max77705.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/maxim,max77705.yaml
@@ -156,6 +156,15 @@ properties:
     minItems: 3
     maxItems: 3
 
+  uno:
+    type: object
+    $ref: /schemas/regulator/regulator.yaml#
+    unevaluatedProperties: false
+    description:
+      The boost on the UNO output, 5 to 9 V with a 0.2 to 1.5 A limit. It
+      powers the wireless charger chip for reverse wireless charging, runs
+      only from the battery, and cannot be on together with USB OTG.
+
   reg:
     maxItems: 1
 
